{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789373038,"nonce":"3/rvvNGTNrfBLhwLPaU4ZKvRLpw=","title":"A constructor call looks its module up by name","message":"`call_constructor_sync` swaps the callee module's variables into the JIT\ncontext before entering the initialiser, and found them with\n`engine.modules.get(name)`: a `HashMap\u003cString, _\u003e` lookup, SipHash over the\nmodule name plus a `memcmp`, on every constructor call. Ash's sampler on\ncaribou's interop bench put it at about 15% of a Wren construct (`hash_one`,\n`Sip13Rounds::write`, `memcmp` under `call_constructor_sync`). The other JIT\nentry points already read the module's `ModuleVarsCell` through\n`module_vars_for(func_id)`, cached per function.\n\nFix: the constructor path reads the cell the same way. Wren→Wren construct\nunder caribou went 33 → 28 ns per call with it; the module name itself is\nstill taken from `func_module` for the context, an `Rc\u003cString\u003e` with no\nhashing.\n\nNoticed beside it, not changed: `collect_garbage` reads\n`WLIFT_VALIDATE_BARRIERS` from the environment on every collection.","files":null}]}